This directory exists so a <link> can point AT A DIRECTORY rather than a file,
which asset-resolve must report differently from "no such file".

It needs this file only because git does not track an empty directory: without
it the directory is absent on a fresh clone, the stat fails, and the test that
asserts the two cases are distinguished sees "no such file" and fails on CI
while passing on the machine that created it. Which is exactly what happened.
